14
00:01:04,489 --> 00:01:10,928
A teammate deletes package-lock.json ("it is generated anyway") and rebuilds:

15
00:01:11,467 --> 00:01:15,173
npm ci refuses to run without a lockfile, by design:

16
00:01:15,173 --> 00:01:21,873
it installs exactly what the lockfile records, so that every build installs the same versions.

17
00:01:21,873 --> 00:01:27,504
npm install would silently resolve the newest versions allowed by package.json,

18
00:01:27,504 --> 00:01:31,995
and two builds of the same commit could contain different code.

19
00:01:31,995 --> 00:01:34,846
The lockfile is part of the source code:

20
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:39,788
Restore the lockfile (in a real project:

21
00:01:39,788 --> 00:01:42,338
git checkout package-lock.json).

22
00:01:42,338 --> 00:01:48,315
If a project really has none, generate it once with Node.js in a container,

23
00:01:48,315 --> 00:01:52,299
without installing Node.js locally, and commit it:

24
00:01:54,033 --> 00:01:54,747
Got it.

25
00:01:54,747 --> 00:01:57,498
What do I need to remember?

26
00:01:58,033 --> 00:02:06,543
Base image pinned, manifests copied first, npm ci --omit=dev from the lockfile, code last.

27
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:13,894
Run as the image's node user, with an exec-form CMD so Node.js receives SIGTERM.

28
00:02:14,433 --> 00:02:16,507
Commit package-lock.json:

29
00:02:16,507 --> 00:02:21,153
without it npm ci fails and builds are not reproducible.

30
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:27,452
I keep hearing about containerizing a Python application.

31
00:02:27,452 --> 00:02:28,969
What is it, really?

32
00:02:29,533 --> 00:02:37,538
How to containerize a Python web API (Flask here; FastAPI works the same way with uvicorn instead of gunicorn):

33
00:02:37,538 --> 00:02:42,874
a slim official base image, pinned requirements installed before the code,

34
00:02:42,874 --> 00:02:46,191
two Python settings that matter in containers,

35
00:02:46,191 --> 00:02:51,023
an unprivileged user, and a production server listening on 0.0.0.0.

36
00:02:51,023 --> 00:02:58,018
The last point is the most common reason a containerized Python app "runs but cannot be reached".

37
00:02:59,767 --> 00:03:03,726
