127
00:10:43,547 --> 00:10:46,298
What do I need to remember?

128
00:10:46,833 --> 00:10:54,482
PHP runs as PHP-FPM (FastCGI, port 9000) behind Nginx (HTTP):

129
00:10:54,482 --> 00:10:58,118
two containers, one job each.

130
00:10:58,667 --> 00:11:05,141
The PHP image contains the code; Nginx reaches it by container name on a shared network.

131
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:08,814
Nginx resolves fastcgi_pass hosts at start-up:

132
00:11:08,814 --> 00:11:13,350
host not found in upstream means the backend is not on the network.

133
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:17,945
Can you show me comparing the stacks?

134
00:11:18,500 --> 00:11:23,526
Lessons 040–044 containerized the same small API in five languages.

135
00:11:23,526 --> 00:11:29,077
Every Dockerfile followed the same principles (official pinned base image,

136
00:11:29,077 --> 00:11:32,377
dependencies before code, unprivileged user,

137
00:11:32,377 --> 00:11:36,953
exec-form start command), but the results are very different,

138
00:11:36,953 --> 00:11:41,453
because each language needs something different at run time.

139
00:11:41,453 --> 00:11:45,879
This lesson builds all five side by side and measures them:

140
00:11:45,879 --> 00:11:50,154
image size, memory in use, and what is inside each image.

141
00:11:51,900 --> 00:11:55,860
First, a fresh practice folder for this lesson.

142
00:11:56,400 --> 00:11:57,574
Build all five.

143
00:11:57,574 --> 00:12:00,468
Each folder is its own build context:

144
00:12:00,468 --> 00:12:06,179
Compare their sizes (--filter reference= selects images by name pattern):

145
00:12:06,733 --> 00:12:11,367
Compare their sizes (--filter reference= selects images by name pattern):

