00:12:11,367 --> 00:12:15,303
Start each one and measure the memory it uses once it is idle:

147
00:12:15,867 --> 00:12:20,380
Start each one and measure the memory it uses once it is idle:

148
00:12:20,380 --> 00:12:25,476
The numbers depend on your machine and versions; the pattern does not:

149
00:12:25,476 --> 00:12:33,847
the Go binary needs a few MB, the JVM and the two gunicorn workers need tens of MB before serving a single request.

150
00:12:33,847 --> 00:12:36,031
The part after / is the limit:

151
00:12:36,031 --> 00:12:42,146
none was set, so it is all the memory of the Docker engine (lesson 098 sets limits).

152
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:45,583
Let me try something.

153
00:12:45,583 --> 00:12:50,069
Java's image is the biggest because it contains the JDK.

154
00:12:50,633 --> 00:12:51,085
javac:

155
00:12:51,085 --> 00:12:56,209
not found, exit code 127 (the shell's code for "command not found"):

156
00:12:56,209 --> 00:13:01,558
the JRE contains the JVM to run Java, but not the compiler to build it.

157
00:13:01,558 --> 00:13:06,229
The Dockerfile compiles inside the image, so it needs the JDK.

158
00:13:06,229 --> 00:13:09,017
The same trap exists for every stack:

159
00:13:09,017 --> 00:13:19,113
a Go binary can run on scratch but scratch cannot compile Go; a Node.js app can run without TypeScript but cannot be built without it.

160
00:13:20,867 --> 00:13:27,070
For now, keep the JDK base (java-api/Dockerfile) and accept the size.

161
00:13:27,070 --> 00:13:34,801
The real fix is to build in a JDK stage and run in a JRE stage of the same Dockerfile:

162
00:13:34,801 --> 00:13:39,296
that is a multi-stage build (lessons 087 and 090).

163
00:13:41,033 --> 00:13:41,747
Got it.

164
00:13:41,747 --> 00:13:44,498
What do I need to remember?

165
00:13:45,033 --> 00:13:51,453
The same principles apply to every stack; what differs is what the application needs at run time.

166
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,981
Measure, do not guess:

167
00:13:53,981 --> 00:13:58,484
docker image ls for size, docker stats for memory.

168
00:13:59,033 --> 00:14:05,233
Build tools (compilers, package managers) are only needed at build time.
